  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their own entry from the parent's `default_map`. The full test suite passes (1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed), including the four new tests.\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/core.py:392`, `Context.__init__` now does `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. Before, it passed the whole parent map down, so a subcommand never found its own keys.\n- **Tests:** I added four to `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n  - a nested subcommand default;\n  - top-level keys not leaking into subcommands;\n  - a group inside a group;\n  - `context_settings` still overriding the inherited map.\n- **Changelog:** I added a `Version 8.5.1 (Unreleased)` entry at the top of `CHANGES.md`. The 8.5.1 number is my guess, so rename it if you version differently. The entry has no issue or PR link, since I don't have numbers.\n\nTop-level keys like `{\"debug\": True}` no longer reach subcommands. Their defaults now have to sit under the subcommand's name.",
